@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** The docstring says both `get` and `put` count as "use", but `get` returned the value without calling `move_to_end`. So after `get("a")`, `"a"` was still marked least recently used and got evicted by the next `put` (caught by `test_get_refreshes_recency`). Fix: call `self._data.move_to_end(key)` before returning the value.
+
+2. **`put` evicted even when updating an existing key.** The capacity check ran unconditionally, so `put("y", 3)` on an already-present key evicted the LRU entry (`"x"`) before overwriting `"y"` in place (caught by `test_updating_existing_key_does_not_evict_others`). Fix: only evict when the key is new (`if key not in self._data and len(self._data) >= self.capacity`).
